Assistant: Before a requester is allowed to close a case early, are there any mandatory waiting periods or minimum time windows that must elapse, and if so what are the exact rules for when closure is permitted or blocked?
User: I don’t have the exact waiting-period rules confirmed yet, so I can’t state a fixed minimum time window with confidence. My expectation is that closure would be blocked while any required reply is still within its allowed response deadline, and only permitted once the requester has either received all expected responses or is explicitly allowed to abandon the case. If there are mandatory grace periods or legal retention windows, those would need to be checked with the business owners or the message specification.

